<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>ToolBench per-domain steering (Gemma 3 4B). Sports fails due to near-synonymous tools.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A.5 </span>NeuronPedia cross-reference</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We cross-referenced our findings with independently labeled features on NeuronPedia<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
          <a href="https://www.neuronpedia.org/gemma-3-4b-it" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.neuronpedia.org/gemma-3-4b-it</a></span></span></span> for Gemma 3 4B-IT. The following pre-existing feature labels align with our discovered circuit stages:</p>
</div>
