<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 20: </span>Base vs instruction-tuned models (%). Effect sizes are large (<math id="A16.T20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\geq 0.71" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.71</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\geq 0.71</annotation></semantics></math>; all exceeding Cohen’s “medium” threshold of 0.5). IT consistently outperforms base; the gap narrows with scale but persists even at 27B.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A16.F13" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.07990v1/fig_base_vs_it.svg" id="A16.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/197;" width="476" height="197"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span>Base vs IT. Left: 5-tool accuracy (base improves with scale but never matches IT). Right: attribution importance (IT is 3–12<math id="A16.F13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> higher).</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A16.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Attribution peak depth</h3>

<figure id="A16.F14" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07990v1/fig_attribution.png" id="A16.F14.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:405/244;" width="405" height="244" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 14: </span>Attribution patching peak layer. IT peaks at 92–98% depth; base models share the location but with much lower importance.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
